# RTK (always on)

**Read and follow** `docs/skills/rtk/SKILL.md` whenever running shell commands.

- If `rtk` is on PATH: prefer `rtk <cmd>` over raw `git` / `ls` / `grep` / `npm test` / etc.
- Need full unfiltered output: `rtk proxy <cmd>` or raw command.
- Missing binary: fall back to raw commands; do not block the task.

Sources: https://github.com/rtk-ai/rtk
